  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Contractors and design firms pay for correct drawings, quantities and schedules. They judge you by accuracy, hand checks and clear communication.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is reading and drawing a plan and section correctly.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and software courses for civil engineering students: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools draft drawings and spot errors. Routine drafting shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Engineering judgment, hand checks and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to explore and check; later, own design decisions.
  </p>

